  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-STANDING-CLEARANCE-FINITE-OVERFLOW-001",
      "severity": "P2 provisional; an admitted extreme finite public clearance query can be reported clear when its segment crosses an ordinary obstacle",
      "classification": "current source trace of the same first failure and example already recorded at recovered checkpoint 059; not a new unique historical defect",
      "detail": "Position::from_metres and its deserializer admit any finite framed coordinates. StandingClearance::new checks projected obstacle bounds, but segment_intersects subtracts the native endpoints into Vec2 without admitting the result, then divides native slab numerators by that delta. Finite endpoint admission does not ensure finite intermediate subtraction. Position::displacement_to owns a checked displacement, but this operation does not use it.",
      "conditional_case": "Use the recovered 059 example, M=f32::MAX; an upright unrotated cuboid centred at (0,0.9,0.5), sized (1,1.8,0.1), with floor 0 gives a finite projected and radius-expanded rectangle near x [-0.8,0.8], z [0.15,0.85]. The affine segment from (-M,0,0) to (M,0,1) crosses that rectangle near t=0.5. In the native slab code, x delta M - (-M) overflows to +infinity, while the two finite near-M x numerators divided by it yield zero. The x interval therefore leaves at 0; the z interval enters at a positive parameter, so the function rejects the intersection and is_clear returns true. This is source and IEEE-arithmetic reasoning, not an executed product operation or an observed plan.",
      "consumer_and_safeguards": "The public API is re-exported from the interior module. Inspected callers use it for short conversation camera offsets, a church door-to-street approach, compound access against fixed obstacles, and access routes against front/rear buildings. Their distinct upstream production and geometry gates do not establish a supported extreme route; the ordinary staged conversation offset is 1.1 m. No generated city, blocked route, rendered scene, gameplay effect or runtime incident is claimed.",
      "connected_scope": "StandingClearance operation admission or robust arithmetic, Position/Displacement ownership, obstruction projection, route and conversation callers, error propagation, zero-length and tangency semantics, and historical aliases.",
      "proposed_repair": "After the audit and implementation authorization, choose a documented robust full admitted-domain computation or a checked/fallible operation policy at the actual slab boundary. Propagate any errors through all actual callers; preserve legitimate zero extents and ordinary route semantics, and avoid compatibility paths or arbitrary restrictions on unrelated geometry.",
      "later_acceptance": "When product validation is authorized, cover this opposite-finite-endpoint example, ordinary short and rotated routes, zero-length segments, inclusive tangency and error propagation through the conversation, church and both property route paths.",
      "historical_related_candidates": [
        "SEGOVB-L13-STANDING-SLAB-FINITE-DIFFERENCE",
        "PL13-055-STANDING-SLAB-FINITE-DIFFERENCE"
      ],
